Yes. Streamlit Community Cloud is the free option, and the plan already has a fallback for it.

Streamlit Community Cloud:

Cost and limits: It’s free, and each app gets up to 2 CPU cores and about 2.7 GB of memory. That’s plenty for this app, since the embedding model is around 130 MB. 
streamlit
Privacy: You can have one private app, so the demo doesn’t have to be public. 
streamlit
Deploying: You connect a GitHub repo, and it redeploys every time you push.
Trade-offs:
It doesn’t use Docker, so the app builds the index the first time it starts. That’s the first-start fallback the plan already includes.
Apps with no traffic for 12 hours go to sleep, so open it a few minutes before your interview. 
streamlit
Settings like the API key go in Streamlit’s secrets settings instead of a .env file.
I’d skip Hugging Face Spaces. It used to be the other free choice, but its docs now say Gradio and Docker Spaces require a paid plan to create. 
huggingface

To be clear, hosting is only one cost. The Anthropic API charges per question no matter where the app runs, but at prototype volume that’s cents, not dollars. The password screen stops strangers from using it.

